  "question": "Can I spray my cotton field tomorrow in Ahmedabad, Gujarat? Also tell me the rain probability tomorrow.",
  "status": "partial",
  "answer": "Task 1: From the Ahmedabad, Gujarat bulletin issued 2026-09-11, for cotton:\n\nCotton · Squaring/ Flowering/ Boll formation · page 3:\n“Sucking pest infestation in cotton at initial stage can be controlled by spraying 500 g of neem seed kernel extract (5% NSKE) or 50 ml of neem oil or a neem-based insecticide by mixing 10 ml (5 EC) to 50 ml (0.03 EC) in 10 litres of water. If the infestation is severe, spray Flonicamid 50 WG with 3 g or Diafenthiuron 50 WP with 10 g or Dinotefuran 20 SG with 3 g by mixing the recommended quantity in 10 litres of water.”\n\nCotton · Squaring/ Flowering/ Boll formation · page 3:\n“To prevent an increase in the population of whiteflies and jassids (leafhoppers), do not use synthetic pyrethroid insecticides until the month of November.”\n\nThese are original English source excerpts, including their conditions. The bulletin is district guidance; it has not been validated for your individual field.\n\nA personal go/no-go decision remains unresolved: field conditions, crop stage and the relevant forecast must be considered. The bulletin alone does not establish that an activity is suitable tomorrow.\n\nTask 2: Ahmedabad · 14 Sep, 00:30–14 Sep, 23:30 IST: Hourly rain chances: 61–95 %. The highest hourly value is 95% for 14 Sep, 15:30–16:30 IST. These percentages are for individual hours, not the chance for the whole day. Source: Open-Meteo best-match forecast; conditions can change.\n\nPart of the request is still unresolved; the missing intervals or tasks are listed below.",
